\newlabel{tab:european-panel-average}{{1}{7}{Average European-option results across the ten-ticker panel. Higher mean gains and higher CVaR$_{5\%}$ values are better; lower bound occupancy is better. Shortfall probability is reported as a secondary distributional diagnostic and should be interpreted jointly with the mean and tail-loss measures}{table.caption.29}{}}
